<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm, soyoil down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm, soyoil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Friday remained firm in central Indian markets and plant delivery condition, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices rose by 50-100 rupees per tonne on good demand from plants against poor arrivals. Arrivals was around 2,000 tonnes in the markets of central India.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained bearish on increased selling from plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 200 rupees per tonne. Business volume was dull and undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were almost steady. Soymeal yellow was $291-292 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $114 for March 15 to 30 shipment and was $111-112 per tonne for April shipment in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,850 rupees for March 15 to 30 and was 3,750 rupees for April delivery in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business was nominal and undertone was steady.</p>
